WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
It's that time again.

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.480
Welcome to Tesla Short's Time, daily episode 512,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.960
coming to you from Vancouver, it's June 16th, 2026.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Let's dive into today's Tesla news.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.820
Tesla's Dojo networking patents move packet recovery

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.440
into hardware so the training fabric keeps running

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.440
even when Ethernet drops frames.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.640
Goldman Sachs raised its second quarter delivery forecast

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.560
for Tesla to 420,000 vehicles.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.380
The firm reviewed registration data

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.360
from the United States, Europe, China, South Korea,

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.920
and Australia before making the change.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.060
The new projection sits above both the earlier 405,000 estimate

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.000
and the street consensus of 400,000.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.900
Full year 2026 deliveries now stand at 1.73 million.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.260
The 2026 earnings per share forecast moved to $1.35

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.080
from $1.30.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.120
The price target stayed at $375, and the rating remained neutral.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.880
The adjustment signals stronger near-term order trends

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.180
without altering longer-term assumptions.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.980
From Wall Street's view of vehicle demand,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.520
we turned to the infrastructure Tesla is building

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.400
to train the autonomy that could change those economics.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.540
Two new patents describe hardware that stores recent packets

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.520
locally and replays only lost segments

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.160
without software intervention.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:36.960
Patent W0204-039-8000, and patent W0204-039-794

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.720
cover the TTPOE approach.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:45.440
The design uses on-chip cash or SRAM as small as 256 kilobytes

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.300
and linked lists to track transmission order.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.180
Four pipeline stages handle stream selection,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.720
link identification, replay or retire decisions,

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:57.220
and pointer updates entirely in hardware.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.600
A hardware link timer working with fiffle memory

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.260
checks multiple links in round robin fashion

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.300
and adapts its tick period.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.100
The system accepts controlled packet loss on Ethernet

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.240
while keeping training jobs from stalling.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.180
Hardware designers usually treat packet loss

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.080
as a problem to eliminate through credits, pauses,

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.420
and lossless fabrics.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.920
Tesla's recent patents instead treat loss

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.160
as an expected event inside a controlled AI cluster

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.940
and move recovery into silicon.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.060
The approach stores recent packets locally,

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.860
tracks order with linked lists and replays

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.900
only the uncertain segment when a timer

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.680
or negative acknowledgement arrives.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.440
Because the decision logic lives in the chip

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.140
rather than the kernel, training jobs avoid the latency spikes

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.460
that software retransmission would introduce.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.440
Every extra millisecond of stall time across thousands

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.460
of GPUs compounds into loss training throughput

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.340
and higher electricity cost per model iteration.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.060
By keeping recovery inside the TTP Mac block

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.400
and adapting the hardware timer to the number of active links,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.460
Tesla reduces that overhead without requiring

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.820
a perfect physical layer.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.740
The trade-off is that the system must still

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.460
guarantee bounded loss rates.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.860
This design choice also reveals a broader pattern

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.340
in Tesla's AI stack.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.220
Rather than buying the most expensive lossless switches,

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.080
the company is optimizing the entire path

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.000
from silicon to software for the specific workload

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.880
of large-scale model training.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.040
While the patents focus on training efficiency,

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.400
Tesla is also preparing the vehicles

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.220
those models will eventually power.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.160
Remember, we covered CyberCab developments yesterday.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.480
EPA filings show the CyberCab carries

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.660
a 48 kilowatt hour battery pack

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.980
and a single front-mounted motor.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:51.260
The documents list estimated range and charging specifications

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.020
that align with a purpose-built robot taxi.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.260
Drone footage captured more than 100 CyberCab vehicles

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.960
parked in formation at Gigafactory, Texas.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.280
The vehicles appear complete and ready for deployment

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.500
rather than in various build stages.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.060
The front-drive layout and modest battery size

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.200
point to lower production cost targets

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.440
than earlier robot taxi concepts.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.460
Production timing and regulatory clearance

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.580
remain the next milestone to watch.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.500
Tesla posted a reminder that its vehicles

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.040
can execute parallel parking autonomously.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.620
The feature uses ultrasonic sensors

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.240
and cameras already present on current models

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.300
to measure the space and steer into it

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.080
without driver input on the wheel.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.020
Owners activate the maneuver through the screen or app.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.600
Once the car has identified a suitable spot,

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:44.180
the post underscores that this capability has been available

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.820
for years yet still surprises some drivers.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.760
As the CyberCab hardware takes shape,

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.420
charging infrastructure for the semi is also being simplified.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.220
Tesla is adapting its plug-and-play supercharger model

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.860
to 1.2 megawatt megacharger sites.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.740
Preassembled units would reduce on-site construction time

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.660
and allow faster expansion of high-power depots.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.360
The move treats charging depots

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.860
as a parallel constraint to vehicle production.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.200
Details on deployment locations and timelines

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.240
are still pending.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.040
While Tesla refines its own hardware and infrastructure,

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.920
a competitor is signaling it will enter the same software lane.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.720
Rivians CEO stated the company plans to launch

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.120
a driver assistance system comparable to Tesla's

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.880
full self-driving before the end of 2026.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:38.360
The announcement positions Rivian as a direct software competitor

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.540
in the same regulatory environment.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.900
No technical specifications or naming for the system were provided.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.320
The timeline places Rivian roughly alongside

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.160
Tesla's push toward unsupervised operation.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:54.080
As more players enter assisted driving,

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.780
real-world safety data from Tesla's limited

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.140
Robotaxi operations becomes relevant.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.120
Tesla's limited Robotaxi operations recorded no

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.020
at fault collisions over four months of supervised

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:07.800
and unsupervised testing.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:12.220
External vehicles struck the test fleet multiple times

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.500
during the same period.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.180
The data covers a small number of vehicles operating

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.640
in controlled conditions.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.140
Regulators will still require larger-scale evidence

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:25.260
before approving broader unsupervised deployment.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.300
While the fleet itself performs cleanly,

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.620
questions are servicing about how regulators

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.360
describe vehicles without traditional controls.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.280
Current EPA and NHTSA terminology

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.500
does not yet address vehicles built

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.200
without steering wheels or pedals.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.340
Tesla's CyberCab and similar programs

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.820
will require new definitions around driver,

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.500
operator, and responsibility allocation.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.100
Updated terminology could affect

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.920
how future safety standards are written and enforced.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.600
The observation comes from an account

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.140
that tracks regulatory filings closely.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.800
Regulatory gaps are one issue.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.440
Another is whether current vision systems

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.680
can handle unexpected cabin conditions.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:11.440
Researchers showed that low-cost doll heads placed

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.800
in the cabin can cause Tesla's occupant detection system

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.800
to misclassify the interior.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:20.500
The test raises questions about edge-case robustness

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.900
in cabin monitoring cameras and software.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.020
Tesla has not yet commented on whether

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:28.320
the finding affects current production vehicles

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.100
or future hardware iterations.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.980
The finding highlights a potential gap

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.940
in current vision-based monitoring

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.300
that could affect both safety features

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.800
and regulatory scrutiny.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.000
SpaceX completed its first Falcon 9 mission

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.080
since the IPO on June 15.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.100
The launch sent 24 Starlink version

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.500
two mini satellites from Vandenberg.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.680
Booster B1093 flew its 14th mission

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:59.520
and lifted off an approximately 834 AM Pacific Daylight time.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.380
The flight was described as routine

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:05.920
yet symbolically significant for the newly public company.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.500
Starlink deployment cadence continues unchanged.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.120
Elon Musk stated that government incentives

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.840
represent less than 2% of the combined enterprise value

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:18.200
of Tesla and SpaceX.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.740
The remark came during a discussion

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.600
of long-term business economics.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.700
It was framed as evidence that both companies

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.360
have moved beyond early-stage reliance on policy support.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.380
It offers a direct counterpoint to narratives

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.640
that treat subsidies as a primary valuation driver.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:39.200
The Tesla Rauti Editor stated a preference

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.280
for a gold-finished cybercab

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.020
once the vehicle reaches customers.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.180
The comment reflects growing anticipation

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.740
around the RoboTaxi's eventual availability

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.400
and customization options.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.860
It also highlights how the vehicle's distinctive design

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.540
is already generating personal ownership interest

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:57.840
beyond fleet use.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:01.340
Insider Monkey aggregates recent institutional

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.440
filings and sentiment indicators around TSLA.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:08.020
The report compiles data from multiple large holders

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.760
without issuing its own price target or rating.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.000
It serves as a snapshot of how professional investors

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.600
have adjusted exposure in the most recent quarter.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.260
An analysis examines how Tesla's

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.900
capital allocation has shifted

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.940
from a lower-priced vehicle program

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:25.060
toward AI and autonomy investments.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:28.640
It quantifies the implied valuation trade-off

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:30.580
between near-term vehicle margins

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:33.340
and longer-term RoboTaxi economics.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.200
The piece notes that current share pricing

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.300
already embeds significant success

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.740
in the autonomy roadmap.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.560
Investors will watch upcoming earnings

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:46.300
for any updated capital expenditure guidance tied to that shift.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.200
Before we go, keep an eye on whether the

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.960
stronger order trends noted by Goldman Sachs

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.500
hold through the end of the quarter in earnings reports.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.300
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

